# Design commands — do not alter visuals

The following UI came from explicit design install commands. **Do not change their visual design, layout, motion, or structure** unless the user explicitly asks to redesign them.

## Locked component sources

- `src/components/ui/glassmorphism-trust-hero.tsx` (easemize glassmorphism-trust-hero) — especially the default `HeroSection` export
- `src/components/ui/modern-stunning-sign-in.tsx` / `modern-stunning-sign-in-demo.tsx`
- `src/components/ui/vintage-keyboard.tsx`
- `src/components/blocks/pricing.tsx` (Codehagen pricing block API + look)
- `src/components/spectrumui/animateddrawer.tsx` (Spectrum / 21st animated-drawer)
- `src/shared/demo.tsx` (drawer demo icons)

## Allowed

- Wire components into pages via **wrappers** (`TrustSection`, `LandingPricing`, `AppShell`, settings, demos)
- Pass product props (Staz plans, OTP handlers, open/close state)
- Fix build/type errors without changing the intended look

## Not allowed without explicit user request

- Restyling colors, spacing, typography, or animations inside locked files
- Replacing the command UI with a simplified/custom redesign
- “Adapting” the design away from the command’s original composition
